{%- comment -%}
  The display title for a collection.

  Shopify's built-in all-products collection is called "Products" and cannot be
  renamed in the admin. On a site that sells competition entries that word is
  wrong everywhere it appears — the h1, the breadcrumb and the browser tab — so
  it is swapped for the brand's own term. Every other collection keeps the title
  the merchant gave it.

  Accepts: collection
  Returns: the title as plain text, ready to escape at the call site.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign title = collection.title
  if collection.handle == 'all'
    assign title = 'collections.all_title' | t
  endif
  echo title
-%}
